WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.460
Such a sad midnight,

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.400
overflowing with love.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:19.970
kiiroi ringo o kajitteru

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.910
Gnawing at a yellow apple,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
kimi wa hitoshirezu otona ni naru

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.930
you secretly become an adult.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
tameiki iro shite mayoikomu

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.370
You sigh, having lost your way

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
ai o sagashite ikiteru

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:31.140
living in a search for love.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
suki yo tabun ne dakedo

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.420
Maybe I love you, but—

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
akai tsuki ga miteru

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.860
the red moon is watching,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
konna ni mo chikaku ni iru no ni

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:45.450
it waits nearby.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
kanashimi sasou midnight

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:49.910
Such a sad midnight.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.980
I can say love

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
koboreru ai o choudai

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.710
It overflows with love.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.710
will you love me?

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
tomadoi no hitomi no oku

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:57.320
Lost within your eyes,

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
kokyuu o tomete

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.270
I stop breathing.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
kimi no ai o katachi ni

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.830
The shape of your love,

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
mayonaka no taiyou

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:08.480
is like the midnight sun.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.210
How is our prisoner Da Ruma doing?

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.950
Um, well, he's oddly calm and relaxed...

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:36.690
Now that the pirate organization he created has come to an end,

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.020
he must feel relieved to be free of all that responsibility.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.160
But didn't the leaders' conference end with the decision

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.460
to not completely destroy the Da Ruma guild?

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:49.570
That's right. We're still rounding up pirates one-by-one, of course,

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:52.470
but there's no need to go and crush the organization itself.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.670
So what we're really doing is try to control other pirate organizations?

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.280
It would be dangerous if all the pirates went into disarray,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.470
so in that respect, guilds are a necessity.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:06.780
The Da Ruma guild's sphere of influence does adjoin Juraian territory

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.290
and Renza Federation territory, after all.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.220
Y-You know about that?

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.060
There's no fooling Principal Mikami, Seto-sama.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.660
Once the Balouta Kingdom is officially recognized by the Union,

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.170
the Da Ruma guild will basically become the Balouta Guild.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.900
And that would put it under Juraian authority, wouldn't it?

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.610
I think I came across as a little aggressive during the meeting,

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:32.180
but it would be best for Balouta to have more territory,

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.310
plus in their eyes it's almost like their native soil.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:37.250
And things will take an even more interesting turn

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.180
If this becomes an opportunity for us to start interacting with Renza!

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.690
But there's one more thing, isn't there?

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:45.710
Yes. Will you take care of the clean-up?

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.690
Once a necessary evil becomes unnecessary, all that's left is the evil.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:55.030
In regards to that, we will need the assistance of the Kuramitsu family.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.600
I humbly ask for your support.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.040
I accept your request.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.010
But I never thought it would become a reality this quickly!

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.550
A unified galactic alliance has started to look less and less like a dream!

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:11.850
But first there is something that must be disposed of.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:18.010
Showdown Between
 Good Luck and 
Bad Luck

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.650
We keep this up and keep getting richer and richer and richer!

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.290
It won't matter how much it costs to rebuild the Da Ruma guild!

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.850
Yes, future commander of the Da Ruma guild!

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:35.100
I am simply working as hard as I possibly can for my client.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.200
I have no such lofty intentions.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.270
Until the day I rescue the president and defeat the vile Seina Yamada,

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:44.110
there will be no respite from my attacks!

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.010
By the way, have you found Seina Yamada?

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:48.450
The Kamidake is presently nowhere to be found...

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.780
It may be because our good luck level is especially high right now.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:56.950
Looks like there's still no rest for the soldiers.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:59.020
But Seto-sama...

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:03.360
Wasn't Tennan-sensei sort of "transferred" to Da Ruma?

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:08.230
It can't be helped. We went and crushed his client's organization.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.960
The end of money is the end of friendship.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.240
Can't we contact the Tennan family directly?

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:20.640
It seems that calling him back home before the contract is up

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:23.550
would result in their having to pay fines for breach of contract.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.710
Poor Tennan-sensei...

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.420
You're stupid to feel sorry for him.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.940
But...

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.290
The Kamidake hasn't encountered the Good Luck Ship once

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.630
since Da Ruma's arrest.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.800
Using the data we obtained from Da Ruma,

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:41.660
simulations say the date we'll run into it next will be...

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:47.570
No good. My male heart doesn't feel a thing...

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:52.180
4 years, 2 months at the longest.

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:53.210
Four years?!

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:57.700
The Kamidake... Lorelei Seina... Don't these matter anymore?

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.090
In any case, we'll need to increase our chances of finding him, and soon.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.620
And I have an idea how.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:07.190
Captain! Message from the supply supervisor.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:09.160
Apparently all of the cargo ships we just captured

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.330
are filled with letters addressed to you.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:13.360
What?

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:17.370
Other pirates have forwarded similar ones to us as well.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.170
Understood. Let me see.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.370
"Letter of Challenge"

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.920
We're going to go that far?!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.150
You know what kind of personality he has.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.320
He would prefer a fancy stage.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.320
Do you think he'll really come?

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:44.120
Don't you worry. He'll come running straight here for sure.

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:49.330
Hey. What's it say?

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.340
If I value President Da Ruma's life, I'm to take the Unko by itself

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:56.170
and fight it out in a one-on-one duel!

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.240
I can't believe you would resort to letters of challenge, Seina Yamada!

00:05:58.240 --> 00:05:59.830
Is there any end to your cowardice?!

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.580
Considering the opponent's personality,

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.620
I suppose it was a good excuse to get him to come, but...

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.850
But that makes us the villains...

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:11.050
Which is why...

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:15.120
Wow, a Power Backhoe! So cool! Hey!

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:15.590
Huh?

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:19.100
Make sure you put up a good fight, Seina-dono.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.060
I'm fighting?!

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.270
Who else is there?

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:25.440
She's got a point.

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.410
The GP's Lorelei Seina is the Da Ruma guild's greatest enemy,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.980
plus that moron has vowed revenge on all Earthlings.

00:06:33.980 --> 00:06:37.710
I can't think of anyone better suited for the job!

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.320
But this is Tennan-sensei we're talking about.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:43.420
Personality aside, his skills are top-notch.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.910
Don't worry. I've prepared a nice instructor for him.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:52.130
Um...! Hey, wait...!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.060
Later!

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.000
By the way, I meant to ask you earlier,

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.940
but what is all this construction and all those spectator seats for?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.010
This is an important fight none should miss.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:08.780
Plus there are lots of people who want to see Seina-dono for themselves.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.710
All advance tickets have already sold out!

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.650
I know it goes without saying, but this definitely smells like a trap.

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:22.290
Curse you, Seina Yamada! You're despicable!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.960
Boy, they really know how to use this guy's personality to their advantage.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.430
So what day is the fight?

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.830
It says on the letters.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:35.100
T-That was the last one...!

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.870
He's so unbelievably stupid...

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:43.650
Uh, shouldn't I be doing sword practice or something?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.850
There's nothing you can learn or master in such a short amount of time,

00:07:46.850 --> 00:07:53.120
much less any special attacks that will ensure your absolute victory.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:56.090
But shouldn't we at least practice or come up with some sort of plan?

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:59.500
Seina-dono. The most important thing in battle is yourself.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.230
"Overcome yourself." is a common enough cliché,

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:06.670
but it also happens to be the best shortcut to improvement.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.670
Nervousness and fear will reduce your skills

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:11.400
to a mere fraction of their normal levels.

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:14.080
So just take it easy!

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:16.110
Won't Seto-sama get mad?

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:20.520
Even that old hag should've expected as much from me.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:21.240
Eh?

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.620
Mikami-sensei.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:27.160
I'm sure there was no mistake in leaving Kanemitsu-sama in charge,

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.190
but I think it might be good for us to come up with something ourselves.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.900
Don't worry. It was an appropriate decision of her.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:33.800
Appropriate?!

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.630
That's the adjective that suits Seto-sama the least.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.270
It isn't that we doubt Seto-sama or Kanemitsu-sama,

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:42.210
but can't we do something too...?

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:44.370
Seina-kun would only feel extra, unnecessary pressure

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.830
if we did things like that.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:54.520
A long time ago, when I was in the Academy, I used to take naps here.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:55.990
Really?

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.760
Yosho and Airi were both pretty childish.

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:02.130
Yosho? Tenchi-senpai's grandfather?

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:06.900
He's since grown up a bit, but Airi hasn't changed at all.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.130
Seina-dono.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.970
When you first came to the Academy,

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.300
did she tell you to let her show you around?

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:13.840
Yeah!

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.670
Now that you mention it, she did say that the classes didn't matter

00:09:16.670 --> 00:09:19.510
so she wanted to show me around on a deluxe tour or something...

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.440
Figured as much.

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:24.710
I told you earlier that you don't need to do anything, but food is essential.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:28.920
You can relieve stress and anxiety just by replenishing your energy.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.250
Eat up!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.880
O-Okay...

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:36.630
Feeling worried?

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.060
Well...

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:40.930
You've already learned basic sword fighting, haven't you?

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:43.430
So that means all that's left are variations of those basic moves.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.800
And it will be a single attack that decides the match!

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:51.110
And besides, actual combat is pretty simple.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:54.310
It's just a clash of basics that both sides have learned.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:57.550
If you're still worried, then just think of it as a fight between two ships!

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.280
You haven't had to fight with swords so much,

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.620
but the number of battles you've been in is nothing to be made light of.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:04.620
That has nothing to do with it.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.920
I'm protected when I'm inside my ship, and everyone else is there too...

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.260
But the same was true for your opponents, wasn't it?

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.560
Eh?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.430
Gimme back my male heart!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.860
"Convention Headquarters"

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:32.860
Seiryo-kun certainly is late.

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:36.390
I don't see how my strategy could fail, but...

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.390
Strange, isn't it?

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:41.590
We know for a fact that he plundered the freighters with all those letters...

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:43.960
Seto-sama! We're receiving a communication.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.430
For me?

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:46.960
I finally found you.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.630
Oh my, how rare this is! Can I help you with something?

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.730
Well, the truth is...

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:53.700
...so he burned all the letters

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:57.270
before checking the date and location of the duel.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:59.380
I'm sorry to bother you, but could you give us the information?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:02.440
Seina Yamada! I'm coming for you!

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:07.980
With the sun down, next comes wine and women.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:08.780
Eh?!

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:10.990
Just leave it to me.

00:11:10.990 --> 00:11:14.220
Everyone from first-timers to obsessed maniacs can enjoy this place
--

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:17.460
And what might "this place" be, Kanemitsu-sama?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:20.060
M-Minaho! What're you doing here?!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:23.300
Seto-sama forgot to mention no alcohol and no women,

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.230
so she asked me to stop by and check up on you.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.070
B-But Seina-dono needs to
--

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.040
I'll tell your wife!

00:11:31.770 --> 00:11:33.840
Hello, Kazuki-sama, Amame-sama!

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:35.440
I didn't see you there!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:37.010
Relax, Kanemitsu-sama.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:40.350
I'm not here to watch over you, I'm just accompanying these two today.

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:41.950
S-Seina-dono.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.350
These are the parents of Azusa-sama, the Juraian emperor.

00:11:45.350 --> 00:11:48.660
I'm Kazuki Yotsuga. Good to meet you, Seina.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.190
I'm his wife Amame.

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.530
I-I'm Seina Yamada!

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.370
Tonight hasn't turned out very well at all...

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:01.470
That husband and wife just now were GP members, weren't they?

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:04.010
So why are they the parents of the Juraian emperor...?

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.680
I'm sorry! I didn't mean to ask something strange like that...

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.480
It's nothing really.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.780
Apparently, Amame-sama had to quit the royal family

00:12:10.780 --> 00:12:13.120
so she could marry Kazuki-sama.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.410
Are you serious...?!

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:21.290
Lots of the Masakis didn't like the royal family lifestyle...

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:23.660
Over time, lots of people have chosen to get out of the family,

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.430
including the sister of the 1st-generation leader.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.060
Yosho too.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:31.130
Listen, members of the Unko.

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:34.640
I am about to put my life on the line to rescue the president.

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.970
It's anyone's guess if I will ever return or not.

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:40.240
But no matter the outcome,

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:45.350
I want you, the crew, to never forget the spirit of the Unko!

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:49.250
Salute Captain Seiryo and 1st Officer Komachi!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.690
I'm counting on you all! Never extinguish the Unko's fire!

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:57.930
Does that mean he wants us to be reckless and desperate?

00:12:57.930 --> 00:12:58.960
I would assume so.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.730
There's nothing we can do - captain's orders.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:09.680
"Battle Arena"

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:09.680
What?!

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:14.440
I'm sorry, all rooms have been booked.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:18.350
But I'm in this show! The leading role, in fact!

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:20.320
Everyone knows that even participants

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.150
must line up for general admission if they arrive late.

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:22.890
I'm telling you, I play the leading
--

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.350
That makes no difference.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.560
What's with this ignorant fool?!

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:29.790
There's nothing we can do. Give it up.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:34.500
Are you really sure you want to trade this ship in for money?

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.330
Yeah! Captain's orders.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:40.100
Apparently he wants us to be reckless and bet it all or something.

00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:46.400
Man, can't wait for tomorrow's fight!

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:51.910
Curse you, Seina Yamada...!

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:56.120
And I went through all that work to put traps in all the hotel rooms...

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:59.460
Trap ceilings, poisonous scorpions, bottomless pits...

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:01.420
I wonder if this is more of his good luck...

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.330
His good luck really hasn't changed all that much

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:07.190
even after stepping off the Good Luck Ship.

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.940
Well, tomorrow's the day...

00:14:12.940 --> 00:14:17.530
Maybe Kanemitsu-san was right; there is no point in thinking about it...

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:22.550
So what dirty tricks are we using tomorrow?

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:25.150
It's going to be a fair-and-square fight.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:29.790
Hold on! That moron will win for sure then!

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:33.590
Don't worry. I have faith in Seina-dono.

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:36.230
What does faith have to do with anything?!

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:41.630
In that case, why don't you bet all of your assets on this match, Seto-sama?

00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.930
OK! I bet on Seiryo-kun, then!

00:14:43.930 --> 00:14:45.630
You old witch!

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.240
I'm sorry to have to say this to you,

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.970
but I think it might be best if Seiryo-kun wins this time.

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:53.640
It seems like his only purpose in life now is to defeat Seina-dono,

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.350
so don't you think maybe he'll come back if we let him do that?

00:14:57.350 --> 00:15:01.980
It would be dangerous if he decided to return to the pirates, after all...

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.520
But when you consider their difference in skill, Seina-kun might get hurt...

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.420
There's no need to worry!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.430
As long as they use Shock Batons instead of real swords,

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.560
he'll wind up with some cuts and bruises at most!

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:16.690
So it's perfectly fine if Seiryo-kun beats Seina-dono's brains out!

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:26.780
My head hurts... Maybe I drank too much last night...

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:29.040
This was all we could buy with the rest of our money...

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.710
Well, our orders were to be desperate and reckless...

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:38.320
To be honest, current odds are 9999-to-1 in Seiryo-sama's favor.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:41.290
So he literally does have a 1 in 10,000 chance.

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:43.160
Amane-chan and the others would be mad

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:45.190
if they found out all proceeds go to charity...

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:48.630
I'll console them if we make a lot of money.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:52.840
Dammit! Thinking about my Seina losing to that idiot pisses me off!

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.970
What do you mean "my"?!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.010
He's my student!

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.910
We can't get in their way; it's a one-on-one duel between two men...

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:03.180
I feel so bad for Big Brother Seina...

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:05.450
I'll have to cheer him up when he gets back.

00:16:05.450 --> 00:16:08.450
I guess that's something to be happy about...

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:10.350
You might be right...

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:13.760
Thanks for sending us tickets like that!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:16.360
We called for tickets the day they went on sale,

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:19.530
but they all sold out before we could get through.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:23.120
It wasn't me. Kiriko-san and the others sent the tickets in my name.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.570
Hello, Seina-sama!

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:29.370
Everyone...!

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:32.340
Seina-sama! I missed you so much!

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:35.140
Please stop!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:40.120
Why aren't I feeling any jealousy at all...?

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.480
A duel, I hear? How cool!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:44.290
Beat him up, okay?

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.760
I'm counting on ya, Seina! Beat him 'till he's numb!

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.160
R-Right...

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:50.350
Um, who might you all be...

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.100
We're Seina-sama's servants!

00:16:54.100 --> 00:16:56.090
A divine duel!

00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:02.140
I will use this Shock Baton to slice, stab, and chop him!

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:05.770
What're you talking about? Are you planning to kill that little boy?

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:07.110
Don't be silly.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:09.880
I need not fight a kid like Seina Yamada with my full strength.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.010
I'll use the back of my sword.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.480
Shock Batons are like the backs of swords, aren't they?

00:17:13.480 --> 00:17:15.350
So you'll only give him some bruises at best.

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.450
You have a point.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:19.790
In that case, I'll use everything I've got to beat him to a pulp!

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.930
Prepare to meet your doom, Seina Yamada!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:27.100
I get the feeling all I've done is put his stupidity into high gear...

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:30.260
Victory is mine! I shall be victorious!

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:40.810
The duel between the GP Academy's Seina Yamada

00:17:40.810 --> 00:17:45.470
and the Da Ruma pirate guild's Seiryo Tennan will now take place!

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.800
Incredible...!

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.300
"Northeast"

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:58.730
Introducing the combatants! From the northeast, Seiryo Tennan!

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:07.940
"Seina (Southwest)"

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:07.940
From the southwest, Seina Yamada!

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:11.540
Good luck, Seina-sama!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.690
Not this situation...!

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:25.920
I pity you, Seina Yamada! You would go to such lengths to ensure victory?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:27.320
Huh?

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.260
You're attempting to use this nostalgic, yet detestable battle scene

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:32.630
to distract me, aren't you?

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.460
But I won't let your plan work!

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:36.770
Um, I'm not really sure what you're talking about...

00:18:36.770 --> 00:18:38.930
I am no longer how I used to be!

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:44.470
Come on! Why didn't anyone realize the duel was about to start?!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.580
You weren't paying attention either, Amane-san!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.880
Come on, let's just hurry!

00:18:48.880 --> 00:18:50.180
Really now...

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:51.310
...so there you have it.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:55.220
I consider this vulgar stage a fitting location for my revenge!

00:18:55.220 --> 00:18:59.460
Not even I can fathom the depths of my power when I've been angered!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:00.790
Hey! Are you even listening to me?!

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.620
Hey, you! Hey!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:04.430
Oh, Komachi-san! It's good to see you again!

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:06.100
You look well!

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:09.600
Say, I know it's a burden, but just play along with him, will you?

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:11.730
No, I'm the one who's been burdening you!

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.770
Seina-kun! Good to see you again!

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:16.210
Oh! Thank you for your help back then!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.240
Let's see, what was your name again...

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.810
Go give it your all!

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:22.510
Thank you!

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.450
Oh! Seina-chan!

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:26.050
Mitoto-san! Hello!

00:19:26.050 --> 00:19:29.050
Did you come to see Seina-chan's duel?

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:31.590
Uh, no, I'm in it...

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:33.710
Oh, my! That's terrible!

00:19:35.260 --> 00:19:39.460
Therefore, there is only one possible, logical outcome...

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:42.360
Your loss to me, Seina Yamada!

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.500
Hey, you!

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:45.930
Pay attention when people are giving you long-winded speeches!

00:19:45.930 --> 00:19:47.440
Oh, sorry...

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:51.170
Give me a break. You aren't even worth my time.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:54.310
But it all ends today.

00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:57.280
By defeating you here in this disgusting setting,

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:03.220
I will forever be free of the coils of fate that bind my body!

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.780
Go, Tennan!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.460
We made it!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:40.680
Here I come!

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:55.430
Ow!

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:21.060
Seina Yamada-dono wins!

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:27.340
Looks like you lose, Seto-sama!

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.890
"Seina Yamada"

00:21:30.340 --> 00:21:33.470
Our desperation and recklessness failed us!

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:41.900
"We apologize for the disturbing footage."

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:44.450
What a pathetic joke.

00:21:44.450 --> 00:21:48.190
The Devil Princess of Jurai, acting in such an arrogant manner...

00:21:48.190 --> 00:21:51.460
But with the Good Luck Ship's clout now gone,

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:54.860
her ship will be going to waste as an ordinary transport ship.

00:21:54.860 --> 00:21:58.770
In that case, we should put it where it best belongs.

00:22:16.240 --> 00:22:27.020
You're the worst, most hopeless,
most unlucky boy in all of space...

00:22:32.260 --> 00:22:34.890
Even against your will...
(You fail.)

00:22:34.890 --> 00:22:36.700
Even when you're gentle...
(You're extremely clumsy.)

00:22:36.700 --> 00:22:41.200
With too much fighting spirit,
in vain, it's all coming to nothing...

00:22:41.200 --> 00:22:44.190
You're gonna fail.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:48.040
Carefully...
(So irritating!)

00:22:48.040 --> 00:22:50.040
Or with violence...
(Ow! Quit it!)

00:22:50.040 --> 00:23:01.110
You're the worst and most hopeless...
you're a lost cause.

00:23:05.560 --> 00:23:10.830
You're the worst and the most hopeless...


00:23:10.830 --> 00:23:15.170
You're an unlucky boy...

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:20.510
But, any way, I'm with you.

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:25.670
So, more and more,
keep on doing what you do!

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.090
The Galactic Army has suddenly sent orders

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:33.960
to have the Kamidake confiscated.

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:36.390
Kiriko-san and the others express their objections,

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.960
but the Kamidake is forcibly taken away anyway...

00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:42.470
No way! I won't let them have Fuku!

00:23:42.470 --> 00:23:44.170
Next time on Tenchi Muyo GXP!

00:23:44.170 --> 00:23:45.160
Pursuit
